frost-dkg serde patch (prerequisite #1)
=======================================
Derives Serialize/Deserialize on `frost_dkg::Participant` so the stateless Lit
Action can seal its DKG participant to its PKP between rounds and replay it.

Against: frost-dkg 0.5.1 (crates.io). Apply from the crate root:
    git apply frost-dkg-serde.patch          # in a frost-dkg checkout
Or upstream it as a `serde` feature / PR (frost-dkg is Lit-authored). The wrapper
crate (../wasm) compiles cleanly with this applied — verified with `cargo check`.

Raw group/scalar fields use the group / prime_field / prime_field_vec serde
helpers from elliptic-curve-tools; wrapped fields carry explicit #[serde(bound)],
mirroring how data.rs already annotates Round1Data.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--- a/src/participant.rs
+++ b/src/participant.rs
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 use super::*;
 use elliptic_curve::group::GroupEncoding;
 use elliptic_curve::{Field, Group};
-use elliptic_curve_tools::SumOfProducts;
+use elliptic_curve_tools::{group, prime_field, prime_field_vec, SumOfProducts};
 use rand_core::{CryptoRngCore, RngCore};
 use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
 use std::collections::BTreeMap;
@@ -45,7 +45,14 @@
 }
 
 /// A DKG participant FSM
-#[derive(Clone)]
+//
+// NOTE (lit-frost-wasm patch): added `Serialize, Deserialize` so the stateless
+// Lit Action can checkpoint its participant between DKG rounds. Raw group/scalar
+// fields use the `group` / `prime_field` / `prime_field_vec` serde helpers, and
+// wrapped fields carry explicit `#[serde(bound(...))]` — mirroring how
+// `Round1Data` is annotated in `data.rs`. Upstream this as a PR / `serde`
+// feature on frost-dkg. See examples/mpc-signing-frost/wasm/frost-dkg-serde.patch
+#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
 pub struct Participant<I, G>
 where
     I: ParticipantImpl<G> + Default,
